WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.111
This example is intentionally incorrect and the
error is useful The

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:10.098
query groups rows only by diagnosis but also tries
to select subject

00:00:10.125 --> 00:00:15.811
ID directly PostgreSQL asks an important question
which subject ID

00:00:15.838 --> 00:00:21.348
should represent the entire diagnosis group There is
no single correct

00:00:21.361 --> 00:00:26.842
subject ID for a group that may contain several
patients Run this

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:32.161
example and read the error message PostgreSQL is
protecting you from an

00:00:32.187 --> 00:00:38.107
ambiguous result To fix a grouped query every
selected expression

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:41.952
needs a clear role It should either define the group
such as

00:00:41.965 --> 00:00:47.496
diagnosis or summarize the group such as COUNT or
AVG Do

00:00:47.522 --> 00:00:52.406
not treat grouping errors as obstacles They often
reveal that the result

00:00:52.432 --> 00:00:54.696
grain has not been defined clearly enough
